IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`

-- sga-part7.l4: Part 7 (sections 59 to 59E) of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Commonwealth),
-- Federal Register compilation C2026C00272, plain-text conversion (not the authorised text).
-- Section 59 (simplified outline) is not a rule and is not encoded; NOTES.md says so.
-- Where the text says the Commissioner "must" or "may" do something "if" conditions are met and they are not, the answer is JUST FALSE; where it is silent, NOTHING.

§ `Section 59A: the notice to pay`

-- src:1105 | (1) This section applies if superannuation guarantee charge payable by an employer is unpaid on the day (the current notice trigger day) that is the day after the end of the 28-day period that started on the day (the imposition day) the charge became payable.
-- src:1106 | Note: The superannuation guarantee charge could be:
-- src:1107 | (a) charge assessed and payable under section 36; or
-- src:1108 | (b) charge in the form of general interest charge payable under section 49.
@ref s 59A(1) (src:1105-1108)
GIVEN `superannuation guarantee charge payable by the employer is unpaid on the current notice trigger day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 59A applies` MEANS
    IF `superannuation guarantee charge payable by the employer is unpaid on the current notice trigger day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- 59A(2): the specified amount must exceed $30 or any higher amount prescribed by the regulations; no earlier notice in the 50-day period ending on the day before the current notice trigger day; no part of the amount in an earlier notice.
-- src:1109 | (2) The Commissioner must, as soon as practicable after the current notice trigger day, give the employer a written notice (the current notice) requiring the employer to pay a specified amount of superannuation guarantee charge if:
-- src:1110 | (a) at least some of the specified amount is the amount referred to in subsection (1); and
-- src:1111 | (b) the remainder (if any) of the specified amount is charge payable by the employer that is unpaid on the current notice trigger day; and
-- src:1112 | (c) the specified amount exceeds $30 or any higher amount prescribed by the regulations; and
-- src:1113 | (d) the employer has not been given an earlier notice under this subsection during the 50-day period ending on the day before the current notice trigger day; and
-- src:1114 | (e) no part of the specified amount has been included in any earlier notice under this subsection.
-- src:1115 | Note 1: As well as including the amount referred to in subsection (1), the amount specified in the current notice could also include:
-- src:1116 | (a) any (other) unpaid general interest charge that has accrued under section 49 since the employer was given the last notice under this subsection; and
-- src:1117 | (b) any (other) unpaid charge that has been assessed under section 36 since the start of the 50-day period mentioned in paragraph (d).
-- src:1118 | Note 2: The employer remains liable to pay the amounts making up the specified amount. The notice does not create a separate liability to pay the specified amount. However, a failure to comply with the notice may result in an administrative penalty under section 59C.
@ref s 59A(2) (src:1109-1118)
GIVEN `at least some of the specified amount is the amount referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the remainder of the specified amount, if any, is charge payable by the employer that is unpaid on the current notice trigger day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified amount` IS A NUMBER
      `any higher amount prescribed by the regulations` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the current notice trigger day` IS A DATE
      `the day the employer was last given an earlier notice under this subsection` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `no part of the specified amount has been included in any earlier notice under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must give the employer a written notice to pay as soon as practicable after the current notice trigger day` MEANS
    IF     `at least some of the specified amount is the amount referred to in subsection (1)`
       AND `the remainder of the specified amount, if any, is charge payable by the employer that is unpaid on the current notice trigger day`
       AND `the specified amount` GREATER THAN threshold
       AND `no earlier notice in the 50-day period`
       AND `no part of the specified amount has been included in any earlier notice under this subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        threshold MEANS
            CONSIDER `any higher amount prescribed by the regulations`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 30
            WHEN JUST higher THEN IF higher GREATER THAN 30 THEN higher ELSE 30
        `no earlier notice in the 50-day period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the employer was last given an earlier notice under this subsection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST d THEN NOT (`a day is in the 50-day period ending on the day before the trigger day` `the current notice trigger day` d)

-- src:1119 | (3) The Commissioner must ensure that the current notice includes words to the effect that an administrative penalty will arise if the employer fails to pay the specified amount during the period (the current notice payment period):
-- src:1120 | (a) starting on the day specified in the notice (which must be on or after the current notice trigger day); and
-- src:1121 | (b) ending on the 28th day after the day specified in the notice.
@ref s 59A(3) (src:1119-1121)
GIVEN `the notice includes words to the effect that an administrative penalty will arise if the employer fails to pay the specified amount during the current notice payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the current notice trigger day` IS A DATE
      `the day specified in the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice meets section 59A(3)` MEANS
    `the notice includes words to the effect that an administrative penalty will arise if the employer fails to pay the specified amount during the current notice payment period`
    AND `the day specified in the notice is on or after the trigger day` `the current notice trigger day` `the day specified in the notice`

-- src:1109 | (2) The Commissioner must, as soon as practicable after the current notice trigger day, give the employer a written notice (the current notice) requiring the employer to pay a specified amount of superannuation guarantee charge if:
-- src:1110 | (a) at least some of the specified amount is the amount referred to in subsection (1); and
-- src:1111 | (b) the remainder (if any) of the specified amount is charge payable by the employer that is unpaid on the current notice trigger day; and
-- src:1112 | (c) the specified amount exceeds $30 or any higher amount prescribed by the regulations; and
-- src:1113 | (d) the employer has not been given an earlier notice under this subsection during the 50-day period ending on the day before the current notice trigger day; and
-- src:1114 | (e) no part of the specified amount has been included in any earlier notice under this subsection.
-- src:1115 | Note 1: As well as including the amount referred to in subsection (1), the amount specified in the current notice could also include:
-- src:1116 | (a) any (other) unpaid general interest charge that has accrued under section 49 since the employer was given the last notice under this subsection; and
-- src:1117 | (b) any (other) unpaid charge that has been assessed under section 36 since the start of the 50-day period mentioned in paragraph (d).
-- src:1118 | Note 2: The employer remains liable to pay the amounts making up the specified amount. The notice does not create a separate liability to pay the specified amount. However, a failure to comply with the notice may result in an administrative penalty under section 59C.
@ref s 59A(2) Note 2 (src:1109-1118)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the notice creates a separate liability to pay the specified amount` MEANS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 59B: a liability is reduced or ceases to exist`

-- src:1123 | (1) If:
-- src:1124 | (a) the current notice payment period has not expired; and
-- src:1125 | (b) a liability under this Act to pay any of the amounts making up the specified amount is reduced (but not to nil);
-- src:1126 | treat the specified amount in the current notice as if it were reduced by the amount of the reduction referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 59B(1) (src:1123-1126)
GIVEN `the day specified in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the specified amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which a liability to pay an amount making up the specified amount is reduced, but not to nil` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the specified amount in the current notice after a reduction` MEANS
    IF `the current notice payment period has not expired on the day` `the day specified in the notice` `the day asked about`
    THEN JUST (`the specified amount` MINUS `the amount by which a liability to pay an amount making up the specified amount is reduced, but not to nil`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1127 | (2) If:
-- src:1128 | (a) the current notice payment period has not expired; and
-- src:1129 | (b) each liability under this Act to pay an amount making up the specified amount either:
-- src:1130 | (i) is reduced to nil; or
-- src:1131 | (ii) ceases to exist;
-- src:1132 | treat the current notice as if it were revoked.
@ref s 59B(2) (src:1127-1132)
GIVEN `the day specified in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `each liability to pay an amount making up the specified amount is reduced to nil or ceases to exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the current notice is treated as revoked` MEANS
    IF `the current notice payment period has not expired on the day` `the day specified in the notice` `the day asked about` AND `each liability to pay an amount making up the specified amount is reduced to nil or ceases to exist`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 59C: the penalty`

-- src:1134 | (1) The employer is liable to pay a penalty if the employer fails to pay the amount specified in the current notice during the current notice payment period.
@ref s 59C(1) (src:1134-1134)
GIVEN `the amount of the specified amount that remains unpaid at the end of the current notice payment period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer is liable to pay a penalty` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the specified amount that remains unpaid at the end of the current notice payment period` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- 59C(2) item 2: the employer became liable for a penalty greater than nil for an earlier notice during the 24-month period ending on the day after the end of the current notice payment period.
-- src:1146 | (a) item 1 does not apply; and
-- src:1147 | (b) the employer has become liable under subsection (1) for a penalty that is greater than nil for an earlier notice during the 24-month period ending on the day after the end of the current notice payment period
-- src:1148 | 50%.
@ref s 59C(2) item 2 (src:1146-1148)
GIVEN `the day specified in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the days the employer became liable under subsection (1) for a penalty greater than nil for an earlier notice` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an earlier penalty falls in the 24-month period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the days the employer became liable under subsection (1) for a penalty greater than nil for an earlier notice`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `either of two possibly unknown conditions holds`
            (`a day is in the 24-month period ending on the day after the end of the payment period` `the day specified in the notice` d)
            (`an earlier penalty falls in the 24-month period` `the day specified in the notice` rest)

-- 59C(2): item 1 (a determination under subsection 18C(4) covers the employer for any part of the period from the imposition day to the end of the payment period): 0%; item 2: 50%; item 3: 25%.
-- src:1135 | (2) The amount of the penalty is equal to a percentage of so much of the specified amount as remains unpaid at the end of the current notice payment period. The percentage is as follows:
-- src:1136 | Percentage used to work out the amount of the penalty
-- src:1137 | Item
-- src:1138 | If:
-- src:1139 | the percentage is:
-- src:1140 | 1
-- src:1141 | a determination is made under subsection 18C(4) covering the employer for any part of the period:
-- src:1142 | (a) starting on the imposition day (see subsection 59A(1)); and
-- src:1143 | (b) ending on the last day of the current notice payment period
-- src:1144 | 0%.
-- src:1145 | 2
-- src:1146 | (a) item 1 does not apply; and
-- src:1147 | (b) the employer has become liable under subsection (1) for a penalty that is greater than nil for an earlier notice during the 24-month period ending on the day after the end of the current notice payment period
-- src:1148 | 50%.
-- src:1149 | 3
-- src:1150 | neither item 1 nor 2 applies
-- src:1151 | 25%.
-- src:1152 | Note: Determinations under subsection 18C(4) cover employers affected by exceptional circumstances. The determination may cover an employer for a period starting before the determination is made.
@ref s 59C(2) (src:1135-1152)
GIVEN `a determination under subsection 18C(4) covers the employer for some part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an earlier penalty falls in the 24-month period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the percentage used to work out the penalty` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a determination under subsection 18C(4) covers the employer for some part of the period` THEN JUST 0
           IF `an earlier penalty falls in the 24-month period` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST 50
           IF `an earlier penalty falls in the 24-month period` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST 25
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1135 | (2) The amount of the penalty is equal to a percentage of so much of the specified amount as remains unpaid at the end of the current notice payment period. The percentage is as follows:
-- src:1136 | Percentage used to work out the amount of the penalty
-- src:1137 | Item
-- src:1138 | If:
-- src:1139 | the percentage is:
@ref s 59C(2) (src:1135-1139)
GIVEN percentage IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that remains unpaid at the end of the current notice payment period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the penalty` MEANS
    (`the amount that remains unpaid at the end of the current notice payment period` TIMES percentage) DIVIDED BY 100

§ `Sections 59D and 59E: assessing and amending the penalty`

-- src:1154 | (1) The Commissioner must make an assessment (a penalty assessment) of the amount of an administrative penalty payable under section 59C by the employer.
@ref s 59D(1) (src:1154-1154)
GIVEN `an administrative penalty is payable under section 59C by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must make a penalty assessment` MEANS
    IF `an administrative penalty is payable under section 59C by the employer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1155 | (2) The Commissioner must give written notice to the employer of the penalty assessment, unless the penalty assessment is nil.
@ref s 59D(2) (src:1155-1155)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must give written notice of the penalty assessment to the employer` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the penalty assessment` EQUALS 0 THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1156 | (3) The penalty becomes due for payment on the day specified in the notice, which must be at least 14 days after the day the notice is given to the employer.
-- src:1157 | Note 1: For provisions about collection and recovery of the penalty, see Part 4-15 in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
-- src:1158 | Note 2: General interest charge does not accrue on any late payment of the penalty.
@ref s 59D(3) (src:1156-1158)
GIVEN `the day the notice is given to the employer` IS A DATE
      `the day specified in the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the penalty is due for payment on the day specified in the notice` MEANS
    `the due day is at least 14 days after the day the notice is given` `the day the notice is given to the employer` `the day specified in the notice`

-- src:1159 | (4) If the employer is dissatisfied with the penalty assessment, the employer may object against it in the manner set out in Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
@ref s 59D(4) (src:1159-1159)
GIVEN `the employer is dissatisfied with the penalty assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer may object against the penalty assessment in the manner set out in Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953` MEANS
    IF `the employer is dissatisfied with the penalty assessment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1156 | (3) The penalty becomes due for payment on the day specified in the notice, which must be at least 14 days after the day the notice is given to the employer.
-- src:1157 | Note 1: For provisions about collection and recovery of the penalty, see Part 4-15 in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
-- src:1158 | Note 2: General interest charge does not accrue on any late payment of the penalty.
@ref s 59D(3) Note 2 (src:1156-1158)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`general interest charge accrues on a late payment of the penalty` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:1161 | (1) The Commissioner must not remit all or a part of the penalty set out in a penalty assessment.
@ref s 59E(1) (src:1161-1161)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may remit all or a part of the penalty set out in a penalty assessment` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:1162 | (2) However, the Commissioner must amend a penalty assessment if:
-- src:1163 | (a) a liability under this Act to pay an amount relevant to the penalty assessment is reduced (including to nil) or ceases to exist; or
-- src:1164 | (b) the amount of the penalty set out in the penalty assessment is reduced to nil because of a determination made under subsection 18C(4).
-- src:1165 | Note: A determination under subsection 18C(4) may cover an employer for a period starting before the determination is made.
@ref s 59E(2) (src:1162-1165)
GIVEN `a liability to pay an amount relevant to the penalty assessment is reduced, including to nil, or ceases to exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty in the penalty assessment is reduced to nil because of a determination under subsection 18C(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must amend the penalty assessment` MEANS
    IF `a liability to pay an amount relevant to the penalty assessment is reduced, including to nil, or ceases to exist` OR `the penalty in the penalty assessment is reduced to nil because of a determination under subsection 18C(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1166 | (3) The amount of penalty payable under the amended penalty assessment is to be worked out in a manner consistent with subsection 59C(2).
@ref s 59E(3) (src:1166-1166)
GIVEN percentage IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that remains unpaid at the end of the current notice payment period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty under an amended penalty assessment` MEANS
    (`the amount that remains unpaid at the end of the current notice payment period` TIMES percentage) DIVIDED BY 100
